WEBVTT

00:02.650 --> 00:03.610
Agnes.

00:04.620 --> 00:06.520
I need you to stay calm and hear me out.

00:06.980 --> 00:09.580
Dear... you look so pale.

00:09.900 --> 00:11.720
Is something the matter?

00:12.330 --> 00:13.580
Y-Yes.

00:14.610 --> 00:16.560
Oh, I know!

00:16.560 --> 00:19.330
You made another extravagant purchase, right?

00:19.690 --> 00:20.960
Listen here, now.

00:20.960 --> 00:23.660
I would never get mad 
over something like that!

00:24.370 --> 00:26.130
All right. What is it?

00:26.870 --> 00:28.720
I... I'm so sorry.

00:29.060 --> 00:30.090
Really, what is it?

00:31.090 --> 00:33.050
I have a new girl in my life!

00:34.430 --> 00:35.130
Huh?

00:38.630 --> 00:39.720
Agnes...

00:40.670 --> 00:44.940
I... I suppose it's not 
such an unusual story.

00:45.250 --> 00:47.230
I am a bit shocked, though.

00:49.320 --> 00:52.110
I didn't mean for it to happen.

00:52.630 --> 00:55.570
I simply became overwhelmed.

00:55.960 --> 00:59.530
W-Well... tell me more about her.

00:59.840 --> 01:00.860
Of course.

01:00.860 --> 01:05.130
She's beautiful, and from 
a high-ranking family.

01:06.020 --> 01:09.270
I see. Sh-She's very charming, then?

01:09.270 --> 01:10.670
And she's a twin!

01:13.140 --> 01:14.510
Casserole!

01:14.510 --> 01:15.910
I-I'm sorry!

01:15.910 --> 01:17.860
I should have gotten 
permission from you first!

01:17.860 --> 01:21.090
And you really think I'd have allowed it?!

01:21.090 --> 01:23.970
Well, Pas agreed to it,

01:23.970 --> 01:27.380
and I think she's more than  
an acceptable match for him...

01:28.890 --> 01:30.150
Pas agreed?

01:30.150 --> 01:30.970
What?

01:30.970 --> 01:32.490
A match... for him?

01:33.980 --> 01:36.400
What did you think I was talking about?

01:36.830 --> 01:39.620
Well... I thought... you were cheating.

01:39.960 --> 01:43.080
Father, how is Mother taking it?

01:44.490 --> 01:45.960
She'll need some time.

01:45.960 --> 01:47.290
She really was shocked, then?

01:48.380 --> 01:50.380
I expect it to last for a month.

01:52.170 --> 01:56.010
<i>Another daughter... I can't wait!</i>

01:58.310 --> 02:03.310
<i>This is the tale of a genius 
patissier who died before his time,</i>

02:03.310 --> 02:07.560
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

02:07.560 --> 02:10.690
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

02:11.570 --> 02:16.300
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

02:17.740 --> 02:24.110
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

03:56.810 --> 04:00.760
<b>County of Retes   Retesvale</b>

03:57.450 --> 04:00.410
Count Retes! Your Ladyship!

04:01.570 --> 04:06.740
<b>Honey for Sweets, and a 
Reservoir for the Villages</b>

04:02.000 --> 04:04.470
So much shouting. What's the meaning of this?

04:04.690 --> 04:08.180
The heir to House Morteln is engaged!

04:09.150 --> 04:12.390
He's been matched with a 
daughter of Margrave Hubarek!

04:12.390 --> 04:14.240
What was that?!

04:14.240 --> 04:15.850
That impoverished backwater knight,

04:15.850 --> 04:17.560
joined to a prestigious noble house?!

04:17.890 --> 04:18.810
Ow!

04:20.250 --> 04:24.490
Ugh! This will leave a stain.

04:24.730 --> 04:27.950
Ahem. Do forgive me.

04:28.250 --> 04:31.170
So? Which girl from House Hubarek?

04:32.830 --> 04:35.770
His fourth daughter, Licorice Mille Hubarek.

04:35.770 --> 04:41.510
Twin sister to Petra, who was recently 
engaged to the grandson of Duke Kadlecek.

04:41.510 --> 04:44.380
The one involved in the kidnapping, you mean?

04:44.380 --> 04:45.720
Yes.

04:45.720 --> 04:50.310
An engagement to prove her chastity 
in the wake of the kidnapping—

04:50.310 --> 04:53.700
At least, such are the 
vulgar rumors being spread.

04:55.560 --> 05:00.090
Is it possible the Hubareks 
intend to wait a few years

05:00.090 --> 05:02.690
until memory of the incident has faded,

05:02.690 --> 05:05.280
and dissolve the engagement then?

05:06.270 --> 05:08.050
I don't think so.

05:09.120 --> 05:14.750
I wonder if Hubarek's true objective is to 
set others at ease regarding their family.

05:15.990 --> 05:17.400
Of course!

05:17.400 --> 05:20.010
The joining with the house 
of Margrave Kadlecek

05:20.010 --> 05:23.710
has significantly increased 
House Hubarek's influence.

05:24.080 --> 05:28.930
So to go in the opposite direction, and bind 
their house to minor one like Morteln...

05:29.240 --> 05:35.640
He's making the case that he's not trying 
to amass power through marriage politics?

05:36.250 --> 05:39.610
It's the kind of thing that 
old fox might think of.

05:40.020 --> 05:41.570
And there's one more thing.

05:41.810 --> 05:47.080
He believes the Fief of Morteln has the 
potential to grow into a bountiful one,

05:47.080 --> 05:48.590
on par with my own.

05:48.590 --> 05:50.500
Surely impossible!

05:50.500 --> 05:52.030
Can you be so sure?

05:52.530 --> 05:56.360
When the land was first granted 
to him twenty years ago,

05:56.360 --> 05:58.370
it was effectively a wasteland.

05:58.820 --> 06:02.210
I've heard it took them several years 
to produce their first harvest.

06:02.630 --> 06:06.100
But over the past three years, 
they reduced their wheat yield,

06:06.100 --> 06:07.880
and began to cultivate beans.

06:08.350 --> 06:09.590
The result?

06:09.950 --> 06:13.090
Using the beans as fertilizer 
to nourish the soil,

06:13.090 --> 06:15.560
they've improved their 
subsequent wheat harvests.

06:15.900 --> 06:17.240
That's true!

06:17.240 --> 06:20.400
And whose idea was that, now?

06:20.400 --> 06:23.530
Could it not have been the suggestion 
of that silver-haired child?

06:23.530 --> 06:27.240
Impossible! He's all of nine years old!

06:27.750 --> 06:32.570
Have you forgotten when they came to 
negotiate compensation for the bandits?

06:33.890 --> 06:38.580
The one conducting the negotiations 
was not Lord Morteln,

06:38.580 --> 06:40.080
but his child.

06:41.080 --> 06:44.120
And he completely got the better of me.

06:45.850 --> 06:50.620
That sly old fox has surely 
noticed the boy's potential.

06:51.030 --> 06:52.540
I've been outmaneuvered.

06:53.010 --> 06:55.970
<b>Village of Le Milotte, Fief of Morteln</b>

07:03.100 --> 07:03.860
There we go!

07:04.160 --> 07:06.480
All right, Lord Pas! That should be it!

07:06.480 --> 07:08.340
Thank you so much!

07:08.790 --> 07:10.910
Pas, what is all this stuff?

07:10.910 --> 07:12.030
Food?

07:12.420 --> 07:17.740
The aid I asked Duke Kadlecek 
and Lord Squale for has arrived!

07:18.170 --> 07:23.460
During the engagement announcement, 
I got them to pledge their support!

07:27.130 --> 07:28.220
What's this thing?

07:28.220 --> 07:29.130
A tree?

07:29.390 --> 07:31.260
It's a black locust sapling.

07:31.260 --> 07:33.090
Also known as pseudoacacia.

07:34.460 --> 07:36.270
Can we eat it?

07:36.270 --> 07:37.430
I'm afraid not.

07:37.960 --> 07:40.140
Can you make black locust pie out of it?

07:40.140 --> 07:41.210
I'm afraid not.

07:41.210 --> 07:42.900
If I did, you couldn't eat it.

07:42.900 --> 07:43.760
Aw...

07:45.550 --> 07:46.390
However...

07:46.390 --> 07:47.020
However?

07:47.240 --> 07:50.340
These trees are easy to grow in poor soil,

07:50.340 --> 07:51.780
and they provide nectar!

07:51.780 --> 07:54.030
Nectar?

07:54.030 --> 07:55.500
Nectar.

07:55.500 --> 07:57.490
It means they can help us make honey!

07:58.700 --> 08:00.060
Honey?!

08:00.060 --> 08:02.150
Honey. The sweet stuff!

08:02.150 --> 08:04.470
Yes, the sweet stuff!

08:04.470 --> 08:08.490
It's so indispensable to the creation 
of sweets across time and location,

08:08.490 --> 08:12.150
any place with a history of 
sweets always involves honey!

08:14.180 --> 08:15.530
We'll raise these trees!

08:15.530 --> 08:17.290
We'll collect honey!

08:17.290 --> 08:19.140
We'll be able to eat sweets!

08:19.140 --> 08:20.750
Yes, correct!

08:20.750 --> 08:22.440
Hooray!

08:22.440 --> 08:26.740
But there are issues with raising them here.

08:26.740 --> 08:27.850
Oh, yeah?

08:27.850 --> 08:29.150
Oh, I know!

08:29.150 --> 08:30.490
Land and water, right?

08:30.490 --> 08:33.110
Right! Excellent deduction!

08:34.370 --> 08:36.110
My grandpa taught me all about it.

08:36.620 --> 08:40.300
The Fief of Morteln gets little rainfall.

08:40.300 --> 08:43.370
Any trees we plant frequently 
die before they're fully grown.

08:43.900 --> 08:46.120
How are we gonna get 'em water, then?

08:46.590 --> 08:48.690
With a shifting of gears.

08:48.690 --> 08:50.940
"A shifting of gears"?

08:50.940 --> 08:52.600
Is that edible?

08:52.600 --> 08:54.160
Certainly not!

08:54.160 --> 08:56.300
It means we change our approach.

08:57.390 --> 09:00.850
There are sweets created from 
a shifting of gears as well.

09:01.270 --> 09:03.710
So, how do we go about that?

09:04.270 --> 09:06.690
Rather than imitating lands 
with plentiful rainfall,

09:07.290 --> 09:11.650
we'll grow them with a method 
common to arid regions.

09:12.200 --> 09:14.200
What method is that?

09:15.780 --> 09:17.570
We'll make a reservoir!

09:18.020 --> 09:19.590
A reservoir?

09:19.590 --> 09:20.220
Can we—

09:20.220 --> 09:21.290
—eat it? No.

09:22.080 --> 09:24.050
It's a place where water collects.

09:24.050 --> 09:29.500
One big enough to last us all year 
round, even the dry early spring!

09:29.500 --> 09:34.940
For that, I chose this 
relatively undeveloped land!

09:35.950 --> 09:41.970
After expenses, profits on the sale of 
textiles comes to eight silver coins.

09:41.970 --> 09:46.130
Wheat comes to fourteen 
silvers and five coppers.

09:46.130 --> 09:49.690
And with the emergency aid earlier...

09:50.630 --> 09:53.150
That's four and three-eighths gold profit.

09:53.150 --> 09:55.400
This concludes last year's earnings report!

09:55.960 --> 09:57.370
Congratulations!

09:57.370 --> 10:01.870
Our efforts have finally 
earned us a full-year profit!

10:02.620 --> 10:05.760
At last. At last, we made it.

10:06.300 --> 10:10.790
It was all pretty touch and go 
when we first came here, right?

10:12.480 --> 10:14.500
Twenty years...

10:15.340 --> 10:16.830
It's had its ups and downs,

10:17.560 --> 10:20.200
but our efforts were finally rewarded.

10:21.240 --> 10:24.790
And the kid played a huge role in that.

10:24.790 --> 10:26.110
Indeed.

10:26.110 --> 10:29.660
Truly, my son is our savior, sent by God!

10:29.660 --> 10:32.430
I wasn't gonna go that far...

10:32.430 --> 10:34.910
Sheesh, what a proud papa...

10:35.320 --> 10:36.250
Feuille...

10:37.790 --> 10:43.030
You, Cointreau, and Glacage 
stayed with me all this time.

10:43.400 --> 10:44.370
I'm so grateful.

10:44.880 --> 10:46.650
Oh, give me a break.

10:46.650 --> 10:51.330
I made the decision to stick with 
you a long time ago, right, boss?

10:51.950 --> 10:55.300
Now, there are two more items to report...

10:55.720 --> 10:58.760
Good news and bad news. 
Which do you want first?

10:58.760 --> 11:00.370
Let me see...

11:00.860 --> 11:02.690
Let's start with the good.

11:02.690 --> 11:05.970
I want to maintain this 
elation for as long as I can.

11:06.210 --> 11:08.250
Figured you'd say that.

11:09.270 --> 11:15.900
Our new village, Le Milotte, has 
gathered over forty settler applicants.

11:16.170 --> 11:18.470
Wow, forty?

11:18.470 --> 11:21.130
Most are refugees,

11:21.630 --> 11:25.460
left with nowhere to go after their 
farms were ravaged by bandits.

11:26.310 --> 11:30.540
If we've got forty, we'll want to 
speed up getting the village in shape.

11:31.030 --> 11:33.230
Well, we got our new infusion of workers.

11:33.230 --> 11:35.250
I think we'll figure it out.

11:35.250 --> 11:37.250
How are those newcomers doing, anyway?

11:37.860 --> 11:42.410
The five we hired with the reward we 
received for handling the Licorice kidnapping?

11:43.000 --> 11:45.120
Glacage is showing them the ropes.

11:46.390 --> 11:47.370
I see.

11:47.810 --> 11:52.890
If having more people means the land grows 
more prosperous, I'll have no complaints.

11:53.520 --> 11:55.860
So? What's the bad news?

11:56.170 --> 11:58.190
This one's big.

11:58.820 --> 12:02.780
I'm told the kid's embarked on a new venture.

12:04.560 --> 12:09.970
I got a report that he headed out to Le 
Milotte with just his little friends.

12:10.450 --> 12:12.270
That mischief-maker!

12:12.710 --> 12:15.420
Can't he ever sit still?!

12:16.820 --> 12:18.650
Feuille! We're going!

12:18.650 --> 12:20.230
Ready when you are!

12:36.230 --> 12:37.050
All right...

12:41.270 --> 12:42.900
Excavate!

12:58.510 --> 13:00.100
What did you do?!

13:00.100 --> 13:01.460
That's awesome!

13:02.500 --> 13:03.920
Amazing.

13:04.750 --> 13:10.390
I'm so glad I secretly 
replicated Strudel's magic!

13:10.940 --> 13:13.130
Pas! That was awesome!

13:13.520 --> 13:15.680
That was magic, right?!

13:18.850 --> 13:20.020
Pas?

13:21.610 --> 13:24.180
This'll work! I can use this!

13:24.180 --> 13:27.370
This spell's way more useful than I expected!

13:29.240 --> 13:32.700
This is the definition of fantastic, right?!

13:32.960 --> 13:37.420
It'll work! It'll work! It'll work!

13:35.610 --> 13:36.880
He's snapped.

13:37.420 --> 13:39.690
Our next suzerain lord has 
totally snapped, yeah.

13:40.230 --> 13:42.630
All right, moving on!

13:43.280 --> 13:44.550
Excavate!

13:46.110 --> 13:47.760
Excavate!

13:49.530 --> 13:50.820
Excavate!

13:50.820 --> 13:54.500
Excavate! Excavate! Excavate! Excavate!

14:00.600 --> 14:02.100
That should do it!

14:02.100 --> 14:03.700
Unbelievable!

14:03.700 --> 14:06.440
Awesome! He did all this himself!

14:07.600 --> 14:11.990
And the floor and walls 
are packed down hard...

14:12.340 --> 14:13.870
That's what makes it a reservoir!

14:14.490 --> 14:18.170
We'll plant the saplings all around it.

14:18.780 --> 14:21.200
It should start raining soon,

14:21.200 --> 14:22.840
so it'll collect water then.

14:23.790 --> 14:30.170
As the trees grow, they'll 
act as reservoirs themselves,

14:30.980 --> 14:33.160
leading to a synergistic effect!

14:35.040 --> 14:36.940
<i>It's all going perfectly!</i>

14:36.940 --> 14:41.810
<i>I could use that excavation spell to 
propel me right to my land of sweets!</i>

14:42.110 --> 14:44.110
<i>No, no! Don't think like that!</i>

14:44.110 --> 14:47.830
<i>In sweets-making, proper process 
and time is of greatest importance.</i>

14:48.200 --> 14:49.320
Pas!

14:49.320 --> 14:50.740
What now?

14:50.740 --> 14:55.480
I'm envisioning a beautiful 
scene beneath my closed eyes.

14:55.800 --> 14:59.440
Well... you might wanna open those eyes.

14:59.440 --> 15:03.330
Huh? What good will opening my eyes...

15:08.190 --> 15:10.970
Pas...

15:13.160 --> 15:16.430
F-Father...

15:16.690 --> 15:19.080
Th-This is...

15:19.540 --> 15:23.400
I thought I'd heard the sound 
of a massive landslide, but...

15:24.010 --> 15:25.780
This is seriously...

15:27.450 --> 15:30.160
I may have overdone it.

15:30.650 --> 15:33.970
Over... done... it?

15:33.970 --> 15:34.880
Tee-hee.

15:36.280 --> 15:39.250
My fool of a son!

15:43.880 --> 15:45.330
That hurt!

15:45.330 --> 15:47.250
Why us too?!

15:48.530 --> 15:50.720
Your Ladyship. Er...

15:54.170 --> 15:57.640
Shall I... freshen up your tea?

15:58.180 --> 16:02.600
Surely you're not still worried 
about House Morteln's connections?

16:03.300 --> 16:07.820
Are you really that concerned 
over the Morteln heir?

16:12.110 --> 16:14.320
If I had a daughter of my own,

16:14.320 --> 16:18.160
I'd have made the same 
decision that old fox did.

16:19.500 --> 16:20.750
Would you?

16:21.150 --> 16:23.390
But what gets under my skin most of all

16:23.390 --> 16:25.460
is that Kadlecek and Hubarek...

16:25.460 --> 16:28.810
Those two easterners ganged 
up to go over my head

16:28.810 --> 16:30.920
and start meddlingin affairs of the south!

16:31.170 --> 16:32.610
Don't they know they should talk to me

16:32.610 --> 16:35.890
before they start poking 
their noses in my business?!

16:38.320 --> 16:39.480
It's gone lukewarm!

16:39.480 --> 16:42.800
Perhaps you should marry him yourself?

16:44.090 --> 16:46.060
F-Forgive me.

16:46.300 --> 16:47.730
It was in jest.

16:48.340 --> 16:53.650
If I were ten years younger, 
or he were ten years older,

16:53.650 --> 16:55.370
I might have tried it, though.

16:57.030 --> 17:00.720
There must be some way to 
take him under my wing.

17:01.610 --> 17:04.460
Shall I refresh your tea?

17:01.610 --> 17:04.460
<b>She took me seriously?</b>

17:11.080 --> 17:13.400
Perhaps that's what I'll try.

17:21.480 --> 17:24.180
It's an excellent irrigation channel.

17:24.180 --> 17:25.690
Isn't it wonderful?

17:25.690 --> 17:27.220
We're so glad to have it!

17:27.220 --> 17:31.350
I'm told Lord Pas created three ponds!

17:31.970 --> 17:33.150
Isn't that amazing?

17:33.150 --> 17:35.920
He made three in less than a month!

17:35.920 --> 17:39.120
Wouldn't it normally take 
at least a month each?

17:39.120 --> 17:43.830
The amazing part was thinking of 
a way to get water without wells

17:44.410 --> 17:47.450
by digging a reservoir for 
irrigation channels...

17:48.840 --> 17:50.280
Hey!

17:51.370 --> 17:53.220
It's Lord Pas!

17:53.590 --> 17:54.820
How does it look?

17:54.820 --> 17:57.340
It's looking great, Lord Pas.

17:57.780 --> 17:59.500
I'm so glad!

17:59.500 --> 18:01.860
We got all the saplings planted, too.

18:01.860 --> 18:03.930
And once we get honey...

18:03.930 --> 18:05.510
We can make sweets!

18:05.510 --> 18:07.080
We can eat!

18:07.080 --> 18:09.170
Yes, correct!

18:09.170 --> 18:10.390
Pas!

18:11.620 --> 18:12.910
Josie?

18:13.290 --> 18:15.030
A letter arrived.

18:15.490 --> 18:16.690
It's for you!

18:17.130 --> 18:18.050
A letter?

18:18.910 --> 18:22.530
It seemed fairly urgent, so I brought it by.

18:23.250 --> 18:25.870
I said I'd bring it, but...

18:26.330 --> 18:29.260
It could be from your cute fiancée!

18:29.260 --> 18:31.530
So as your sister, I took responsibility.

18:31.530 --> 18:34.530
Wh-What are you talking about?!

18:37.820 --> 18:40.000
Th-This is...

18:42.000 --> 18:43.940
From your fiancée after all?

18:44.330 --> 18:46.720
From Count Retes.

18:46.960 --> 18:48.760
Count Retes?

18:48.760 --> 18:49.940
What in the world?

18:50.900 --> 18:53.900
It's an invitation to a tea tasting ceremony.

18:54.710 --> 18:57.180
"I was hoping to receive..."

18:58.490 --> 19:01.600
"...your opinion on our new teas."

19:01.600 --> 19:03.910
"I'll be waiting."

19:05.670 --> 19:08.330
The count asked for me, specifically?

19:08.990 --> 19:11.350
She's up to something.

19:13.530 --> 19:17.050
Once that's over, we'll have to figure 
out how to manage the grain storage.

19:17.650 --> 19:21.860
<b>New Retainer  Nicolo Nono</b>

19:18.840 --> 19:22.250
Why's there so much to do?!

19:22.750 --> 19:24.480
Don't complain.

19:24.480 --> 19:28.470
I thought I'd be able to take 
it easy out here in the sticks!

19:28.700 --> 19:30.640
I feel you, okay?

19:30.640 --> 19:36.150
It's that little demon who's 
got us busy as hell here.

19:36.150 --> 19:38.190
You misunderstand, Feuille.

19:38.560 --> 19:39.760
Kid!

19:39.760 --> 19:41.780
Everything that happens in Morteln is

19:41.780 --> 19:45.660
under the authority of my 
father, the liege lord.

19:46.170 --> 19:50.800
In other words, it's my father 
who's the reason you're busy.

19:50.800 --> 19:56.880
And who, exactly, went over that 
authority's head to dig a reservoir?

19:57.160 --> 20:00.340
As next liege lord, I was 
acting on his behalf.

20:00.790 --> 20:03.570
You've got a real smart mouth, you know?

20:03.570 --> 20:04.960
Aw, shucks!

20:04.960 --> 20:06.450
That wasn't a compliment!

20:06.450 --> 20:08.670
If you've got complaints, 
direct them at this guy!

20:08.670 --> 20:10.810
Go on! Really tell him off!

20:10.810 --> 20:13.060
R-Right...

20:13.780 --> 20:17.270
By the way, is Father not here?

20:17.690 --> 20:20.580
He flew off. Business at the royal capital.

20:20.580 --> 20:22.690
He's not back yet.

20:22.690 --> 20:24.240
Oh, really?

20:24.750 --> 20:27.200
Something you need to talk to him about?

20:27.720 --> 20:33.410
The truth is, Count Retes invited 
me to a tea tasting ceremony.

20:33.660 --> 20:35.460
You specifically?

20:35.770 --> 20:36.510
Yeah.

20:37.280 --> 20:39.360
I'm pretty sure she's plotting something.

20:39.670 --> 20:41.850
That does seem likely.

20:41.850 --> 20:44.560
I wanted to talk to Father about it, but...

20:44.930 --> 20:46.970
I know all about it.

20:48.330 --> 20:50.130
I heard in the royal capital.

20:50.130 --> 20:52.430
From someone other than Count Retes.

20:52.790 --> 20:54.470
What could she be up to?

20:55.070 --> 20:59.900
Does she want revenge for how I handled 
the bandit compensation negotiations?

21:00.300 --> 21:02.860
We can talk about that later.

21:03.230 --> 21:06.510
Pas, I've brought an important guest.

21:06.510 --> 21:07.570
Guest?

21:12.370 --> 21:13.870
Lady Licorice!

21:16.330 --> 21:17.930
Lord Pastry!

21:18.900 --> 21:20.660
Oh, I mean...

21:20.660 --> 21:22.350
Just Pastry.

21:22.350 --> 21:24.220
I've been hoping to see you again.

21:24.220 --> 21:26.210
Oh, right.

21:26.210 --> 21:29.170
Licorice, I'm happy to see you, too.

21:29.690 --> 21:32.300
A visit from the fiancée, eh?

21:32.300 --> 21:33.770
Lucky you.

21:33.770 --> 21:35.530
Not merely a visit.

21:36.890 --> 21:41.360
Circumstances necessitate that I 
impose on you for the time being.

21:42.120 --> 21:43.370
Impose?

21:43.710 --> 21:46.860
You mean... you'll be living here?

22:03.090 --> 22:03.870
Huh?

23:37.050 --> 23:39.160
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.160 --> 23:42.350
"Sweet or Bitter? The Tea Tasting Ceremony."

23:39.160 --> 23:45.060
<b>Sweet or Bitter? The Tea Tasting Ceremony</b>

23:42.350 --> 23:43.810
Bon appétit!

23:45.060 --> 23:50.250
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:45.060 --> 23:50.250
<b>Chako Abeno</b>
